<title>USA: Keystone International Q4 shr profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Keystone International Q4 shr profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr profit	$0.33	   loss   $0.16</p>
<p> Net profit	11,800	  loss   5,500</p>
<p> Net Sales	 176,800		  159,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  35,600		   35,400</p>
<p>	  YEAR</p>
<p> Shr		 $1.18		    $0.56</p>
<p> Net		 41,900		   19,900</p>
<p> Net Sales	 677,900		  597,100</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  35,500		   35,400</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Fourth quarter and full year 1995 were affected by unusual items including restructuring, asset impairment, severance and plant closure charges as well as certain nonrecurring gains.</p>
<p>Severance and related costs for Q4 1995 were $14.4 million and $22.8 million for the year. Impairment of assets held for sale amopunted to $8.2 million in Q4 1995 and the same for the full year. Plant closures and related costs amounted to $2.9 million for full 1995.</p>
<p>Excluding those items, Q4 1995 net income would have been $10 million or $0.28 per share.</p>
</text>
